// `std.authority`: the ambient authority. `std` reaches the host by
// capability, on `cap-std`'s design (`../README.md`): authority enters a
// program in one place, as `main`'s parameter, `def main(authority :
// Authority)`, and never through a global. That is what
// `cap_std::ambient_authority()` marks in Rust, and `gandr run` hands it to
// `main` once. Each host module's root capability is attenuated from it: a
// capability holding more operations stands where one holding fewer is asked,
// and a holder never reaches an operation its own does not hold. The authority
// holds the operations of every host module of the map that has landed, and
// grows by each one that lands.

/// The ambient authority: every host operation a landed module of `std`
/// reaches, held once, as `main`'s parameter.
pub type Authority = Cap { print, eprint, read_line };

/// The standard streams' root capability, opened from `authority`.
pub def console(authority : Authority) -> Cap { print, eprint, read_line } {
  authority
}
